# Shell scripts and the git hook keep LF line endings on every checkout, Windows
# included. Git for Windows checks text files out with CRLF by default
# (core.autocrlf=true). Its own bash runs such a script anyway; any other sh reading
# the same working copy (WSL, a Linux container, a Mac on a shared drive) takes each
# CR as part of a command and stops at the hook's `set -e` ("set: Illegal option -").
*.sh            text eol=lf
scripts/hooks/* text eol=lf
